From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SaaSD3v <noreply@github.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 00:45:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: fix smbchg_check_temp_state null return

smbchg_check_temp_state() returns an int, but its NULL guard uses a bare
return. It also dereferences chip while initializing temp_state before the
NULL guard runs.

Validate chip before dereferencing it and return the existing
POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_UNKNOWN state for the invalid-input case. This keeps the
normal path unchanged while making the function valid for Clang 11.
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-smbcharger-mmi.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-smbcharger-mmi.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-smbcharger-mmi.c
index 782f6e5aa919..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-smbcharger-mmi.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom/qpnp-smbcharger-mmi.c
@@ -3361,10 +3361,13 @@ static char *smb_health_text[] = {
 static int smbchg_check_temp_state(struct smbchg_chip *chip, int batt_temp)
 {
 	int hotspot;
-	int temp_state = chip->temp_state;
+	int temp_state;
 
 	if (!chip)
-		return;
+		return POWER_SUPPLY_HEALTH_UNKNOWN;
+
+	temp_state = chip->temp_state;
 
 	mutex_lock(&chip->check_temp_lock);
 
-- 
